ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE ACT ON RESTORATION OF HONOR AND COMPENSATION FOR VICTIMS OF SAMCHEONG EDUCATION

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on Restoration of Honor and Compensation for Victims of Samcheong Education and matters necessary for its enforcement. <Amended on December 30, 2005>

Article 2 (Diseases Related to Samcheong Education)
"Diseases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2, subparagraph 2 (b) of the Act on Restoration of Honor and Compensation for Victims of Samcheong Education (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means diseases that the Subcommittee for Determining Medical Treatment Periods and Disability Grades under Article 6 (1) 2 recognizes as eligible for compensation and medical assistance payments. <Amended on December 30, 2005>

Article 3 (Composition and Operation of the Committee for Deliberation on Restoration of Honor and Compensation for Victims of Samcheong Education)
(1) Members of the Committee for Deliberation on Restoration of Honor and Compensation for Victims of Samcheong Education under Article 3 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee") shall be commissioned or appointed from among persons with extensive knowledge and experience in relevant fields and public officials at director-general level or higher belonging to the Ministry of Justice, the Ministry of National Defense, the Ministry of Patriots and Veterans Affairs, and the National Police Agency who are designated by the heads of the respective agencies. <Amended on April 11, 2023>
(2) The chairperson of the Committee shall convene meetings of the Committee and preside over them.
(3) Where the chairperson is unable to perform duties for an unavoidable reason, a member designated in advance by the chairperson shall act on behalf of the chairperson.
(4) Meetings of the Committee shall be opened with a majority of the members in office present, and resolutions shall be adopted with the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present.

Article 4 (Matters for Deliberation and Resolution by the Committee)
"Other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree in connection with restoration of honor and compensation, etc. for victims or bereaved family members" in Article 3 (1) 6 of the Act means the following matters:
1. Matters concerning fact-finding investigations, etc. under Article 17 of the Act;
2. Details concerning the composition and operation of subcommittees under Article 6;
3. Other major matters related to restoration of honor and compensation, etc.

Article 5 (Administrative Staff of the Committee)
(1) The Committee shall have one secretary and the necessary staff to handle its affairs.
(2) The secretary shall be appointed by the chairperson from among State public officials of Grade III or IV of the Ministry of National Defense or public officials in general service belonging to its Senior Civil Service. <Amended on December 30, 2005; June 12, 2006>
(3) The secretary shall handle the affairs of the Committee under the orders of the chairperson and may attend and speak at meetings of the Committee.
(4) The staff assigned to the Committee pursuant to paragraph (1) may be filled by public officials seconded from relevant central administrative agencies.

Article 6 (Composition of Subcommittees)
(1) The Committee shall establish the following subcommittees:
1. The Subcommittee for Examining Eligibility as Victims and Bereaved Family Members, which handles duties under Article 3 (1) 1 of the Act;
2. The Subcommittee for Determining Medical Treatment Periods and Disability Grades, which handles duties under Article 3 (1) 3 of the Act.
(2) Each subcommittee shall consist of not more than 10 members appointed or commissioned by the chairperson from among persons with extensive knowledge and experience and State public officials in general service of Grade III or IV or public officials in general service belonging to the Senior Civil Service of relevant central administrative agencies (including public officials in specific service or special service of equivalent rank); the chairperson of each subcommittee shall be appointed by the chairperson of the Committee from among members of the Committee. <Amended on June 12, 2006>

Article 7 (Allowances)
(1) Members attending meetings of the Committee and subcommittees may be paid allowances within budgetary limits: Provided, That this shall not apply where a member who is a public official attends in direct connection with his or her official duties.
(2) Witnesses or persons giving information who appear before the Committee, etc. pursuant to Article 17 of the Act may be paid travel expenses and actual expenses within budgetary limits.

Article 8 (Application of Average Monthly Wages)
(1) The monthly salary, actual monthly income, or average wage under Article 4 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "average monthly wage") shall be based on certification by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu (the head of a Gu means the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply) or the head of a tax office having jurisdiction over the victim's domicile, or other reliable certification.
(2) Where there is no documentary evidence concerning the average monthly wage under paragraph (1), the average monthly wage shall be the monthly salary or daily labor wage based on nationwide statistics by sex surveyed by occupation by a wage survey institution that periodically publishes wage statistics at least once each year: Provided, That where nationwide statistics are unavailable, the daily labor wage based on regional statistics of the Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, or Do having jurisdiction over the victim's domicile at that time shall apply.
(3) The average monthly wage under paragraph (2) shall be based on the statistics in the Ministry of Employment and Labor's Report on the Basic Statistical Survey of Wage Structure; where basic wage structure statistics are unavailable, it shall be based on the National Data Agency's statistics on unit construction labor costs, and where statistics on unit construction labor costs are also unavailable, it shall be based on the monthly salary or daily labor wage of ordinary laborers by sex surveyed using a reliable method: Provided, That the minimum wage shall be the average wage by sex for 1980 based on the statistics in the Ministry of Employment and Labor's Survey Report on Wages by Occupation. <Amended 2010.7.12, 2025.10.1>

Article 9 (Deduction of Living Expenses)
Living expenses to be deducted from the average monthly wage pursuant to Article 4 (5) of the Act shall be the living expenses calculated according to the table of ratios of the deceased person's own living expenses in Attached Table 7 of the Enforcement Decree of the State Compensation Act. <Amended 2005.12.30>

Article 10 (Medical Assistance Payments)
Medical assistance payments, including medical treatment expenses, nursing care expenses, and expenses for the purchase of assistive devices, under Article 5 (1) of the Act shall be the amounts calculated by the following methods: <Amended 2021.9.29, 2025.10.1>
1. Medical treatment expenses shall be the amount calculated on the basis of an estimate of medical treatment expenses issued by a national general hospital, a hospital affiliated with a medical college (excluding branch hospitals), or a hospital designated by the Committee (hereinafter referred to as "designated hospitals, etc."): Provided, That where designated hospitals, etc. recognize the need for medical treatment expenses but are unable to estimate them, the amount shall be determined by the Committee in consideration of the opinion of the Subcommittee for Determining Medical Treatment Periods and Disability Grades and medical treatment expenses in similar cases;
2. Where a medical certificate issued by designated hospitals, etc. establishes that, even after full recovery, the victim has a physical disability that makes it difficult to engage in activities without the care of another person, nursing care expenses shall be the amount obtained by multiplying the amount determined by the Committee, in consideration of the opinion of the Subcommittee for Determining Medical Treatment Periods and Disability Grades, within a range from a maximum of 990,000 won to a minimum of 330,000 won per month, by the average remaining life expectancy periodically published by the National Data Agency as of the date on which the Act enters into force;
3. Where a medical certificate issued by designated hospitals, etc. establishes the need to wear assistive devices, expenses for the purchase of assistive devices shall be the amount obtained by multiplying the number of purchases deemed necessary during the average remaining life expectancy, according to the useful life of the assistive devices, by the market purchase price.

Article 11 (Application for Payment of Compensation, etc.)
(1) A person who intends to apply for payment of compensation or medical assistance payments under Article 8 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "compensation, etc.") shall submit to the Committee, through the head of a Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over the applicant's domicile, an application for payment of compensation, etc. in Attached Form 1 or Attached Form 2, together with the following documents, within the application period publicly announced pursuant to Article 20: <Amended 2005.12.30, 2006.6.12, 2010.11.2>
1. Deleted <2006.6.12>
2. One copy of a certificate of matters recorded in the victim's family relations register or a certified transcript of a removed family register (limited to cases where verification cannot be made through a certificate of matters recorded in the family relations register and the applicant is a bereaved family member of a deceased, missing, or injured person);
3. One copy of a document selecting a representative of the bereaved family members in Attached Form 3 (limited to cases where a representative of the bereaved family members has been selected);
4. One copy of a power of attorney for receipt of compensation, etc. in Attached Form 4 (limited to cases where an application is made through an agent due to emigration, hospitalization, or other unavoidable grounds);
5. One copy of a certificate of occupation and monthly salary in Attached Form 5 (limited to persons earning employment income);
6. One copy of a certificate of occupation and actual monthly income in Attached Form 6 (limited to persons earning business income);
7. One copy of other supporting materials that may substantiate the grounds for the application.
(2) In applying for and receiving payment of compensation, etc. under paragraph (1), where the applicants are bereaved family members of a deceased, missing, or injured person and there are 2 or more heirs to property of the same priority, a representative of the bereaved family members shall be selected using the document selecting a representative of the bereaved family members in Attached Form 3: Provided, That this shall not apply where it is impossible for the heirs to property of the same priority to reach agreement.
(3) Where a person who intends to apply for payment of compensation, etc. pursuant to paragraph (1) is unable to apply for or receive compensation, etc. in person due to emigration, hospitalization, or other unavoidable grounds, the person may appoint an agent by means of a power of attorney for receipt of compensation, etc. in Attached Form 4, confirmed by any of the following persons:
1. The head of a diplomatic mission abroad, in cases of a stay abroad, such as emigration;
2. The head of the relevant medical institution, in cases of hospitalization;
3. The head of the relevant custodial institution, in cases of confinement in a correctional institution, etc.;
4. The head of the Eup/Myeon/Dong of the person's domicile, in other cases.
(4) Where the relevant documents specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) are not attached, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu who receives an application for payment of compensation, etc. under paragraph (1) shall require the applicant to supplement the application with those documents.
(5) The Committee that receives an application for payment under paragraph (1) shall verify a certified copy of the applicant's resident registration record through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act: Provided, That where the applicant does not consent to verification, the Committee shall require the applicant to attach that document. <Amended 2010.11.2>

Article 12 (Matters Concerning Restoration of Honor, etc.)
(1) The matters on which the Committee shall deliberate and resolve concerning the restoration of honor of victims or bereaved family members shall be as follows:
1. Recommendations to expunge records of academic disciplinary action against victims related to Samcheong Education, reinstate them in school, or award them honorary diplomas;
2. Recommendations to employers to reinstate victims who were dismissed from employment in connection with Samcheong Education;
3. Other matters recognized by the Committee among the matters for which restoration of honor has been requested.
(2) No victim shall be subjected to any discriminatory treatment or disadvantage by the State, local governments, employers, etc. on the grounds that the victim underwent Samcheong Education.
(3) A person who intends to apply for restoration of honor under paragraph (1) shall submit to the Committee, through the head of a Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over the applicant's domicile, an application for restoration of honor in Attached Form 7, together with the following documents: <Amended 2005.12.30, 2006.6.12, 2010.11.2>
1. Deleted <2006.6.12>
2. One copy of a certificate of matters recorded in the victim's family relations register or a certified transcript of a removed family register (limited to cases where verification cannot be made through a certificate of matters recorded in the family relations register and the applicant is a bereaved family member of a deceased, missing, or injured person);
3. One copy of other supporting materials that may substantiate the grounds for the application.
(4) Article 11 (3) through (5) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the procedures for applying for restoration of honor under paragraph (3). <Amended 2006.6.12>

Article 13 (Requests for Reexamination, etc.)
Where a special reason exists, the chairperson of the Committee may request the relevant subcommittee to conduct a reexamination or make a new determination with respect to an examination or determination by a subcommittee under Article 6.

Article 14 (Decisions)
Where the Committee makes a compensation decision or a decision on restoration of honor, it shall prepare a written compensation decision in attached Form 8 or a written decision on restoration of honor in attached Form 9, stating the following matters, etc., and all members present at the Committee meeting shall sign the written decision or enter their names and affix their seals thereto:
1. The applicant's name, address, and resident registration number;
2. The operative part of the decision;
3. The grounds for the decision;
4. The year, month, and day of the decision.

Article 15 (Notification)
Where the Committee makes a compensation decision or a decision on restoration of honor, it shall retain the original written compensation decision or written decision on restoration of honor and serve on the applicant two authenticated copies of the written compensation decision or written decision on restoration of honor and the relevant notice of decision (a notice of compensation decision in attached Form 10 or 11, or a notice of decision on restoration of honor in attached Form 12 or 13). Where the applicant has an agent, these documents shall be served on the agent, and one certified copy of the written compensation decision or written decision on restoration of honor shall be served on the applicant.

Article 16 (Applications for Reconsideration)
A person seeking reconsideration under Article 11 of the Act shall submit to the Committee an application for reconsideration in attached Form 14, accompanied by the following documents, within 30 days from the date of service of the written compensation decision:
1. One copy of a certificate of physical (mental) disability diagnosis in attached Form 15 issued by designated hospitals, etc. (limited to cases where the applicant objects to the determination of the disability grade);
2. One copy of other supporting materials capable of proving the grounds for reconsideration.

Article 17 (Consent and Claims for Payment)
Where an applicant who has received a notice of compensation decision or a notice of decision on restoration of honor under Article 15 wishes to receive payment of compensation, etc. or obtain restoration of honor pursuant to a decision on restoration of honor, the applicant shall submit to the Committee a consent and claim form in attached Form 16 stating the following matters, accompanied by one authenticated copy of the written compensation decision or written decision on restoration of honor and one copy of the applicant's certificate of registered seal:
1. The applicant's name, address, and resident registration number;
2. The receipt number and operative part of the compensation (restoration of honor) decision;
3. A statement that the applicant consents to the compensation (restoration of honor) decision and claims payment of compensation, etc.;
4. A copy of the account passbook at a financial institution through which compensation, etc. may be received;
5. The year, month, and day of the claim.

Article 18 (Paying Agency)
Compensation, etc. determined by the Committee shall be paid by the Committee, but the practical processing of payment may be entrusted to the National Treasury (including National Treasury agents).

Article 19 (Time of Payment)
Compensation, etc. shall be paid within 15 days from the date a claim for payment under Article 17 is made.

Article 20 (Public Notice)
The chairperson of the Committee shall publicly announce the following matters concerning applications for compensation and restoration of honor in the Official Gazette and at least two daily newspapers within 30 days from the date this Decree enters into force:
1. Persons eligible for compensation;
2. Qualifications of applicants;
3. The agency receiving applications;
4. The application period;
5. Standards for calculating compensation, etc.;
6. Procedures for deliberation and decision;
7. Required documents;
8. Other matters necessary for applications and payment.

Article 21 (Fact-Finding Investigations)
(1) Where the Committee is unable, through its own investigation, to verify the facts concerning the information in an application submitted under Articles 11 and 12, it may notify the Minister of National Defense, the Commissioner General of the National Police Agency, or other relevant officials of that information and have its veracity verified.
(2) The Minister of National Defense, the Commissioner General of the National Police Agency, or other relevant officials who have verified the veracity of the information in an application under paragraph (1) shall record the details in a certificate confirming admission to Samcheong Education and harm suffered in attached Form 17 and notify the Committee thereof, together with supporting documents.

Article 22 (Applications for Project Expenses by Related Organizations)
Where a related organization intends to apply for project expenses, etc. under Article 19 of the Act, it shall submit the following documents:
1. Articles of incorporation or organizational rules;
2. A list of members;
3. Minutes of the regular general meeting for the relevant year (including budget and settlement of accounts documents);
4. A project plan.

Article 23 (Detailed Enforcement Rules)
Matters necessary for the enforcement of this Decree shall be prescribed by the chairperson following a resolution of the Committee.

